  "notes": {
    "rm110": "seeds_cached is the maintained entity index (entity_cache); a real Engine read adds one durable projector-mark read (get_offset). The benchmark stub keeps that mark constant.",
    "engine_search_after": "Of the ~120-136 ms p50, about 115 ms is the RM-88 caller check calling storage.get_record once per admitted edge (122 lookups): the synthetic world has no source records, so none is in the read's record set. The graph part (seeds + leg) is read_path_after. Batch record lookup is a separate follow-up, not RM-110.",
    "rm96": "walk_d2 now applies QUALIFIED_WALK_FRONTIER_CAP=16 and QUALIFIED_WALK_DEEP_MAX_DEGREE=16 on levels >= 2; walk_d2_uncapped lifts both. Hub seed reach 1511 -> 201 nodes; depth-1 walks unchanged. LadybugDB frontier_edges costs 11-24 ms per query even for 6 rows (its OR predicate scans the relationships); a UNION of two anchored MATCHes measured hub 24 -> 14 ms, 16-node frontier 41 -> 27 ms (scratch probe, not applied: adapter left to the GraphStore merge).",
    "neo4j": "live neo4j:5 container at bolt://localhost:57689, stopped afterwards; the Engine end-to-end read was run on SQLite and LadybugDB only."
  }
